+              description: |
+                The node has received a block (from P2P or API) that is successfully imported on the fork-choice `on_block` handler.
+                This includes valid imported blocks that do not become the head. The event does not wait for an execution payload envelope to be received.
+
+                Before Gloas, `builder_index` and `block_hash` are absent. From Gloas onwards, both fields are required and contain
+                `signed_execution_payload_bid.message.builder_index` and `signed_execution_payload_bid.message.block_hash` from the imported block.
+                `builder_index` is a quoted decimal uint64. `block_hash` is the `0x`-prefixed 32-byte execution block hash, not the beacon block root in `block`.
+                Self-built blocks also include both fields, with `builder_index` set to `BUILDER_INDEX_SELF_BUILD` (`"18446744073709551615"`).
+                The existing `slot`, `block`, and `execution_optimistic` fields are unchanged.
